t. Total snow\naccumulations between 12 and 18 inches, with locally higher amounts\npossible. Winds gusting as high as 45 mph.\n\n* WHERE...Northwest San Juan Mountains and Southwest San Juan\nMountains.\n\n* WHEN...Until noon MST Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be very difficult to impossible. The\nhazardous conditions will impact the Monday morning commute.","ends":"2026-11-02T12:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b284c983150236c87728b60844c957442b4b55be.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b284c983150236c87728b60844c957442b4b55be.001.1"},{"event":"Winter Weather Advisory","headline":"Winter Weather Advisory issued November 1 at 7:52PM MST until November 2 at 6:00PM MST by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Snow expected above 10000 feet. Total snow accumulations\nbetween 5 and 10 inches. Locally higher amounts possible. Winds\ngusting as high as 35 mph.\n\n* WHERE...Flat Tops, Gore and Elk Mountains/Central Mountain Valleys,\nGrand and Battlement Mesas, and West Elk and Sawatch Mountains.\n\n* WHEN...Until 6 PM MST Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be very difficult.","ends":"2026-11-02T18:00:00-07:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"Grand and Battlement Mesas; Gore and Elk Mountains/Central Mountain Valleys; West Elk and Sawatch Mountains; Flat Tops","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b284c983150236c87728b60844c957442b4b55be.003.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b284c983150236c87728b60844c957442b4b55be.003.1"},{"event":"Avalanche Advisory","headline":"Avalanche Advisory issued October 31 at 7:16PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"SABCO\n\nTHE FOLLOWING MESSAGE IS TRANSMITTED AT THE REQUEST OF THE\nCOLORADO AVALANCHE INFORMATION CENTER.\n\n...A SPECIAL AVALANCHE ADVISORY IN EFFECT FROM 4:30 PM SATURDAY\nUNTIL 4:30 PM MONDAY...\n\n*WHAT...Avalanche conditions are dangerous above treelin